===============================================
Tcpdump
===============================================
tcpdump is a packet capture tool used to inspect network traffic at a very low level — TCP flags, handshakes, retransmissions, resets, everything.


👉 Works mainly at OSI Layer 3 & 4


===============================================
1️⃣ Basic TCP Capture (most used)
===============================================
tcpdump -i eth0 tcp


Captures all TCP traffic on eth0.


===============================================
2️⃣ Capture TCP traffic for a specific port
===============================================


tcpdump -i eth0 tcp port 443

Used when debugging:

HTTPS
PostgreSQL (5432)
SSH (22)


===============================================
3️⃣ Capture traffic between two hosts
===============================================

tcpdump -i eth0 tcp and host 10.0.0.5
--> It captures only TCP network packets on interface eth0 that are sent to or received from 10.0.0.5.

Or very precise:

tcpdump -i eth0 tcp and src host 10.0.0.5 and dst port 5432

===============================================
4️⃣ TCP 3-Way Handshake Troubleshooting
===============================================

Healthy handshake looks like:
SYN
SYN-ACK
ACK

Command
tcpdump -i eth0 tcp port 80 -nn

What you might see
✅ Normal
SYN
SYN-ACK
ACK

❌ Issue: SYN but no SYN-ACK
SYN
SYN
SYN


💡 Problem:

Firewall blocking

Port closed

Security group / NACL issue (AWS)


===============================================
5️⃣ Debug “Connection refused”
===============================================

tcpdump output:
SYN
RST


💡 Meaning:

Server reachable

But nothing listening on that port

👉 Check:

ss -lntp


===============================================
6️⃣ Debug “Connection timeout”
===============================================


tcpdump output:
SYN
(no response)


💡 Meaning:

Packet dropped

Firewall / routing issue

Security group / NACL / network ACL


===============================================
7️⃣ Debug TCP Reset (RST)
===============================================


tcpdump -i eth0 'tcp[tcpflags] & tcp-rst != 0'

RST means:

App crashed

Load balancer closed connection

Idle timeout exceeded

Very common with:

ALB idle timeout

Backend app crashes


===============================================
8️⃣ Debug TCP Retransmissions (packet loss)
===============================================

tcpdump -i eth0 tcp


Look for:

Retransmission
Dup ACK


💡 Meaning:

Network congestion

Packet loss

MTU issues

===============================================
9️⃣ Capture and Analyze Later (production-safe)
===============================================
tcpdump -i eth0 tcp port 443 -w capture.pcap


Then analyze with:

Wireshark

tshark


===============================================
🔟 Debug Slow TCP Connections
===============================================


Check:

Long gaps between packets

Multiple retransmissions

Window size shrinking

👉 Often caused by:

CPU throttling

App slowness

Network latency


===============================================
TCP Flags Cheat Sheet
===============================================
| Flag | Meaning          |
| ---- | ---------------- |
| SYN  | Start connection |
| ACK  | Acknowledge      |
| FIN  | Graceful close   |
| RST  | Force close      |
| PSH  | Push data        |



===============================================
1️⃣ Basic tcpdump line anatomy
===============================================
12:01:22.123456 IP 10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [S], seq 123456, win 64240, length 0



How to read it

12:01:22.123456 → Timestamp

IP → Layer 3 protocol

10.0.0.5.54321 → Source IP + source port

> → Direction

10.0.0.10.80 → Destination IP + port

Flags [S] → SYN

seq → Sequence number

win → TCP window size

length 0 → No payload (normal for SYN)

===============================================
2️⃣ Healthy TCP 3-Way Handshake (ideal case)
===============================================

10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [S]
10.0.0.10.80 > 10.0.0.5.54321: Flags [S.]
10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [.]

Meaning

[S] → SYN

[S.] → SYN-ACK

[.] → ACK

✅ Connection established successfully

===============================================
3️⃣ Firewall / Security Group Blocking (SYN retry loop)
===============================================

10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [S]
(retries)
10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [S]

What this tells you

Client is sending SYN

Server never responds

❌ Network drop
👉 AWS SG / NACL / firewall / routing issue

===============================================
4️⃣ Port Closed (Connection Refused)
===============================================
10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [S]
10.0.0.10.80 > 10.0.0.5.54321: Flags [R.]

Meaning

Server is reachable

Port not listening

👉 Check:

ss -lntp | grep 80

===============================================
5️⃣ Application Crash / Forced Close (RST mid-connection)
===============================================

10.0.0.5.54321 > 10.0.0.10.80: Flags [.], length 512
10.0.0.10.80 > 10.0.0.5.54321: Flags [R.]

Meaning

Connection was established

Server suddenly reset

👉 Causes:

App crash

ALB idle timeout

Pod restart (K8s)

===============================================
6️⃣ Slow Network / Packet Loss (Retransmissions)
===============================================
Flags [.], seq 1000:1500
Flags [.], seq 1000:1500 (retransmission)
Flags [.], seq 1000:1500 (retransmission)

Meaning

ACK not received

TCP resending packets

👉 Causes:

Packet loss

MTU mismatch

Network congestion

===============================================
7️⃣ TCP FIN – Graceful Connection Close
===============================================
Flags [F.]
Flags [.]
Flags [F.]
Flags [.]

Meaning

Normal, clean shutdown

Nothing to worry about

===============================================
8️⃣ TIME_WAIT symptom (not tcpdump but important)
===============================================

You’ll often see:

New connections fail

tcpdump shows handshake but app can’t connect

Check:

ss -ant | grep TIME-WAIT | wc -l


===============================================
9️⃣ Common tcpdump Flags Cheat Sheet
===============================================

| Flag   | Meaning   |
| ------ | --------- |
| `[S]`  | SYN       |
| `[S.]` | SYN-ACK   |
| `[.]`  | ACK       |
| `[F.]` | FIN       |
| `[R.]` | RST       |
| `[P.]` | PSH + ACK |




